{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445934-fighting-style-in-gauru-ie-kung-fu-panda","id":445934,"title":"Fighting Style In Gauru? ie. Kung Fu Panda?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T08:23:58-07:00","id":445934,"title":"Fighting Style In Gauru? ie. Kung Fu Panda?","content":"Relentless Assault specifically states in can be used in Gauru form. <br /> <br /> My question is: <br /> <br /> Can I use Heavy Blade Fighting, Light Blade, Close Quarters Combat, Cheap Shot, and so on while in Gauru form? What about Kung Fu? Defensive Fighting? <br /> <br /> I would think the Rage would keep those things from being possible, such as Cheap Shot (quick groin strike or spit in the eye while Raging?), and especially things like Guns in general, let alone a firearms based fighting style?<br /> <br /> Is Relentless Assault the exception, not the rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:35:08-07:00","id":446048,"title":"","content":"The rule that they cannot appears to have vanished for 2e. Also the text of relentless assault just sort of mentions offhand that it's better in gauru or urshul, without making a big deal that it works at all in the former.<br /> <br /> So I think you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:35:09-07:00","id":446049,"title":"","content":"Fathers form makes it more plausible, and the martial arts training would help master the rage as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:38:02-07:00","id":446052,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't attacking with the weapon unleash the rage though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:45:19-07:00","id":446062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445934-fighting-style-in-gauru-ie-kung-fu-panda?p=446052#post446052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't attacking with the weapon unleash the rage though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would. So you might get a few rounds of Kung fu Panda in before the Killer Panda comes out to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:51:38-07:00","id":446069,"title":"","content":"In 1e, it was explicitly the case.<br /> <br /> 2e didn't repeat that Fighting Merits were out in Gauru form or during Rage. Though the Rage has specific restrictions on what you're doing. A lot of Fighting Merits (styles or not) are going to be out simply because they're not attacks. <br /> <br /> I think 2e got away from the flat rule in favor of case-by-case sense; and because having Merits geared to fighting in Gauru is cool and not having to specify that they work around a rule each time is also better.<br /> <br /> But I have no idea if they meant to completely remove some of the restrictions 1e had in place (esp. regarding things like weapon choice).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:53:08-07:00","id":446409,"title":"","content":"I believe they did. I think a lot of forsaken 2's creation is geared towards what's fun. The main rule of this dev team seems to be never say no. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T00:54:38-07:00","id":447353,"title":"","content":"Well on a case by case basis I could outlawing certain maneuvers, but really, there should never be the case where a forsaken is less dangerous in their killing form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:22:54-07:00","id":447588,"title":"","content":"As long as they are following the basic instinctive drive of Gauru to attack, I don't see the problem. Most of the Armed Defense and Unarmed Defense stuff is going to be worthless; but having a Gauru werewolf grapple someone wearing armor while using Close Quarters Combat 3 to make that Armor work against them right before biting their head off? Yeah, absolutely. Some other effects are straight up pointless, or redundant: Martial Arts 4 lets you do Lethal; a werewolf in Gauru already does Lethal. Martial Arts 5 gives you +2 damage bonus for unarmed attacks. I <i>don't</i> think this should stack; it should instead probably just mean that even when the Gauru wolf is punching something with his knuckles instead of tearing at it with his claws, it should still be +2L.<br /> <br /> A small tangent: anyone else feel like Martial Arts 4 and 5 work better if they're switched? +2B at MA 4 and <i>then</i> Lethal damage at MA 5 seems much more appropriate in terms of escalation. First you learn how to hit a lot harder--then you learn how to murder with your knuckles. It also helps me envision how boxing would work: I can see a boxer having +2B, but not doing L. It makes the longer fights more plausible, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 03-18-2015, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T15:32:44-07:00","id":448372,"title":"","content":"I probably won't let players use any maneuver in Garou form. It seems unthematic to me to use anything but teeth and claws while Raging. Besides, werewolves have magic teeth even before adding the effects of Gifts which are going to be better than most weapons they'd have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T15:38:16-07:00","id":448379,"title":"","content":"Heavy Weapons style with a bigass klaive seems thematic enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T15:56:10-07:00","id":448394,"title":"","content":"Relentless Assault is of course made for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:56:14-07:00","id":448541,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say that maneuvers that don't break the &quot;attack every turn&quot; mandate are fine. I'm iffy on finesse based attacks, but that may be bias based on expectations from the previous edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:09:55-07:00","id":449064,"title":"","content":"As long as you are meeting the requirements for the Rage restriction, you are free to use Fighting Styles and Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:47:34-07:00","id":450721,"title":"","content":"I do like this change. Thanks for clarifying this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5351-dapperdog","name":"DapperDog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}